    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "s = \"abcd\", k = 2                    ->  \"abcd\"   (nothing to remove)\ns = \"deeedbbcccbdaa\", k = 3          ->  \"aa\"\ns = \"pbbcggttciiippooaais\", k = 2    ->  \"ps\""
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The idea: a stack of runs"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Removing a group can make **new** neighbours meet — and they may complete another group. Rescanning the whole string after each removal works but is slow. A stack does it in one pass, because the only thing that can grow is the run just before the current letter: the **top** of the stack."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Store each run as a pair **[letter, count]**. A letter equal to the top run increases its count; when the count reaches `k`, pop the whole run — and the run underneath becomes the top, ready to be extended by the next letter. A different letter starts a new run."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Brute force: scan, remove, repeat"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function removeDuplicates(s, k) {\n  let changed = true;\n  while (changed) {                           // repeat until a pass removes nothing\n    changed = false;\n    for (let i = 0; i + k <= s.length; i++) {\n      let j = i;\n      while (j < s.length && s[j] === s[i] && j - i < k) j++;\n      if (j - i === k) {                      // k equal letters start at i\n        s = s.slice(0, i) + s.slice(i + k);   // cut them out and start again\n        changed = true;\n        break;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n  return s;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def remove_duplicates(s, k):\n    changed = True\n    while changed:                        # repeat until a pass removes nothing\n        changed = False\n        for i in range(len(s) - k + 1):\n            if s[i:i + k] == s[i] * k:    # k equal letters start at i\n                s = s[:i] + s[i + k:]     # cut them out and start again\n                changed = True\n                break\n    return s"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "String removeDuplicates(String s, int k) {\n    boolean changed = true;\n    while (changed) {                            // repeat until a pass removes nothing\n        changed = false;\n        for (int i = 0; i + k <= s.length(); i++) {\n            int j = i;\n            while (j < s.length() && s.charAt(j) == s.charAt(i) && j - i < k) j++;\n            if (j - i == k) {                    // k equal letters start at i\n                s = s.substring(0, i) + s.substring(i + k);   // cut them out and start again\n                changed = true;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return s;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "string removeDuplicates(string s, int k) {\n    bool changed = true;\n    while (changed) {                            // repeat until a pass removes nothing\n        changed = false;\n        for (size_t i = 0; i + k <= s.size(); i++) {\n            size_t j = i;\n            while (j < s.size() && s[j] == s[i] && (int)(j - i) < k) j++;\n            if ((int)(j - i) == k) {             // k equal letters start at i\n                s.erase(i, k);                   // cut them out and start again\n                changed = true;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return s;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n² / k), space O(n).** There can be n / k removals, and each one rescans and rebuilds the string."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. A stack of [letter, count] runs"
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "remove-duplicates-ii",
      "caption": "Each run sits on the stack with its length; reaching k pops it and lets the run below grow again."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function removeDuplicates(s, k) {\n  const stack = [];                           // [character, how many in a row]\n  for (const ch of s) {\n    const top = stack[stack.length - 1];\n    if (top && top[0] === ch) {\n      top[1]++;                               // one more of the same letter\n      if (top[1] === k) stack.pop();          // k in a row: they vanish together\n    } else {\n      stack.push([ch, 1]);\n    }\n  }\n  return stack.map(([ch, n]) => ch.repeat(n)).join(\"\");\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def remove_duplicates(s, k):\n    stack = []                            # [character, how many in a row]\n    for ch in s:\n        if stack and stack[-1][0] == ch:\n            stack[-1][1] += 1             # one more of the same letter\n            if stack[-1][1] == k:\n                stack.pop()               # k in a row: they vanish together\n        else:\n            stack.append([ch, 1])\n    return \"\".join(ch * n for ch, n in stack)"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "String removeDuplicates(String s, int k) {\n    Deque<int[]> stack = new ArrayDeque<>();     // {character, how many in a row}\n    for (char ch : s.toCharArray()) {\n        if (!stack.isEmpty() && stack.peek()[0] == ch) {\n            if (++stack.peek()[1] == k) stack.pop();   // k in a row: they vanish together\n        } else {\n            stack.push(new int[]{ch, 1});\n        }\n    }\n    StringBuilder out = new StringBuilder();\n    Iterator<int[]> it = stack.descendingIterator();   // bottom of the stack first\n    while (it.hasNext()) {\n        int[] run = it.next();\n        for (int i = 0; i < run[1]; i++) out.append((char) run[0]);\n    }\n    return out.toString();\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "string removeDuplicates(string s, int k) {\n    vector<pair<char, int>> stack;               // {character, how many in a row}\n    for (char ch : s) {\n        if (!stack.empty() && stack.back().first == ch) {\n            if (++stack.back().second == k) stack.pop_back();   // k in a row: they vanish together\n        } else {\n            stack.push_back({ch, 1});\n        }\n    }\n    string out;\n    for (auto& [ch, n] : stack) out.append(n, ch);\n    return out;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n), space O(n).** Each letter is pushed or counted once and popped at most once."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing the approaches"
    },
    {
      "type": "complexity",
      "rows": [
        {
          "approach": "Brute force: scan, remove, repeat",
          "time": "O(n² / k)",
          "timeWhy": "Up to **n / k** removals, each **rescanning and rebuilding** the string.",
          "space": "O(n)",
          "spaceWhy": "The rebuilt string."
        },
        {
          "approach": "A stack of [letter, count] runs",
          "time": "O(n)",
          "timeWhy": "Each letter is **pushed or counted once** and popped at most once.",
          "space": "O(n)",
          "spaceWhy": "The stack of runs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Storing a **count** with each stack entry is the trick to remember: it turns *\"are the last k letters equal?\"* from a k-step check into a single comparison."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Nothing to remove** — the string comes back unchanged.",
        "**Chain reactions** — removing one group creates the next (`\"abbbaaca\"`, k = 3 → `\"ca\"`).",
        "**A run longer than k** — `\"aaaa\"` with k = 3 leaves `\"a\"`: the count restarts after each removal.",
        "**k longer than the string** — no group can ever form: the string comes back unchanged."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Variations"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Remove All Adjacent Duplicates in String** — the k = 2 case, where a plain stack of letters is enough (Stack course).",
        "**Candy Crush (1D)** — remove runs of 3 or more, not exactly k: pop when the run *ends* with a count of at least 3.",
        "**Make The String Great** — a letter and the same letter in the other case cancel: the same push/pop with a different match rule."
      ]
    }
  ],
